---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
    <div class="content article-page">
        <div class="card">
            <h1>The Biggest Merge War in MyProfitLand</h1>
            <p class="meta">Author: <span>Mina Boles</span> | Published on Feb 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
  <img class= "article-image" src="imgs/IMG_6769.jpeg" alt="">
            <p>
                One of the fiercest wars in <strong>MyProfitLand</strong> history took place between <strong>Palestine</strong> and <strong>El Salvador</strong>. This merge war tested strategy, resource management, and endurance. The battle was extremely close, with only a few million points separating the sides despite hundreds of heavy strikes.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>War Overview</h2>
            <p>
                The war started with Palestine initiating the attack for territorial control. Both sides relied heavily on nuclear strikes, supported by ballistic missiles and chemical bombs. The confrontation was intense and required careful coordination.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Strike Statistics</h2>
            <table class="strike-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Strike Type</th>
                        <th>Palestine</th>
                        <th>El Salvador</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Nuclear Bomb (4,000,000 Damage)</td>
                        <td>62</td>
                        <td>64</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Ballistic Missile (300,000 Damage)</td>
                        <td>53</td>
                        <td>48</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Chemical Bomb (150,000 Damage)</td>
                        <td>4</td>
                        <td>6</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Total Strikes</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>119</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>118</strong></td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Final Power</h2>
            <p>
                - Palestine power before the merge: 326,099,079<br>
                - Palestine power after the merge: 322,837,155<br>
                - Final difference: 3,261,924 points
            </p>
            <p>
                The war ended in a complete merge of the region, showing how evenly matched both sides were.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Why This War is Legendary</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Largest number of nuclear strikes in a direct confrontation.</li>
                <li>Extremely close balance in total power until the end.</li>
                <li>High density of strikes from both sides.</li>
                <li>Victory determined by a very small margin after massive resource usage.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h2>Conclusion</h2>
            <p>
                The merge war between Palestine and El Salvador was not just a battle of strength, but a test of strategy and endurance. The narrow final difference makes it one of the most memorable and intense wars in MyProfitLand history.
            </p>
        </div>
</div>
</Layout>
